# LEARN FIRST CONSTRUCTOR LIKE (__init__) METHOD

 __init__() - is a constructor.
 It automatically calls when you create an object for the class.
 Object is instance of class.


 #__init__(self)
 is a constructor method that runs automatically when a new object is created.
 It is used to initialize object data.

 #self -> this keyword in java
 self refers to the current object, allowing each object to store and access its own data.


 #object
 An Object is an instance of a Class.
 It represents a specific implementation of the class and holds its own data. An object consists of

State: It is represented by the attributes and reflects the properties of an object.
Behavior: It is represented by the methods of an object and reflects the response of an object to other objects.
Identity: It gives a unique name to an object and enables one object to interact with other objects.
